    {
      "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1053a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1053A Persons taken to be members of regulated superannuation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022c00235#sch-1-sec-1053a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2022c00235.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2022c00235.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "funds and approved deposit funds and holders of RSAs\n\nFor the purposes of this Division, each of the following persons is\ntaken to be a member of a regulated superannuation fund or an\napproved deposit fund, or a holder of an RSA, (as the case\nrequires):\n\n(a) a non-member spouse in relation to whom a splitting order\nunder the Family Law Act 1975 has been made, from the day\non which a copy of the order is served on the trustee of the\nfund;\n\n(b) a non-member spouse who is a party to a superannuation\nagreement under the Family Law Act 1975, from the day on\nwhich a copy of the agreement is served on the trustee of the\nfund;\n\n(c) a party to a marriage in relation to which an order of a kind\nreferred to in Part VIIIAA of the Family Law Act 1975 has\nbeen made, if the order relates to an interest in the fund;\n\n(d) an eligible person, within the meaning of section 90MZB of\nthe Family Law Act 1975, in relation to an interest of the\nmember or holder in the fund;\n\n(e) a covered ADF member within the meaning of the Australian\nDefence Force Cover Act 2015.\nSubdivision B—Powers of AFCA",
      "skos:definition": "funds and approved deposit funds and holders of RSAs\n\nFor the purposes of this Division, each of the following persons is\ntaken to be a member of a regulated superannuation fund or an\napproved deposit fund, or a holder of an RSA, (as the case\nrequires):\n\n(a) a non-member spouse in relation to whom a splitting order\nunder the Family Law Act 1975 has been made, from the day\non which a copy of the order is served on the trustee of the\nfund;\n\n(b) a non-member spouse who is a party to a superannuation\nagreement under the Family Law Act 1975, from the day on\nwhich a copy of the agreement is served on the trustee of the\nfund;\n\n(c) a party to a marriage in relation to which an order of a kind\nreferred to in Part VIIIAA of the Family Law Act 1975 has\nbeen made, if the order relates to an interest in the fund;\n\n(d) an eligible person, within the meaning of section 90MZB of\nthe Family Law Act 1975, in relation to an interest of the\nmember or holder in the fund;\n\n(e) a covered ADF member within the meaning of the Australian\nDefence Force Cover Act 2015.\nSubdivision B—Powers of AFCA",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1053a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1053a-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1053a-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1053a-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1053a-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1053a-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bf986f606cb010592e3193d7b5a8b57ebeb465cd48fd48ecd063895ed906a633",
      "skos:note": "Persons taken to be members of regulated superannuation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022c00235#sch-1-sec-1053a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1053A Persons taken to be members of regulated superannuation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 24,
      "values:originalText": "funds and approved deposit funds and holders of RSAs\n\nFor the purposes of this Division, each of the following persons is\ntaken to be a member of a regulated superannuation fund or an\napproved deposit fund, or a holder of an RSA, (as the case\nrequires):\n\n(a) a non-member spouse in relation to whom a splitting order\nunder the Family Law Act 1975 has been made, from the day\non which a copy of the order is served on the trustee of the\nfund;\n\n(b) a non-member spouse who is a party to a superannuation\nagreement under the Family Law Act 1975, from the day on\nwhich a copy of the agreement is served on the trustee of the\nfund;\n\n(c) a party to a marriage in relation to which an order of a kind\nreferred to in Part VIIIAA of the Family Law Act 1975 has\nbeen made, if the order relates to an interest in the fund;\n\n(d) an eligible person, within the meaning of section 90MZB of\nthe Family Law Act 1975, in relation to an interest of the\nmember or holder in the fund;\n\n(e) a covered ADF member within the meaning of the Australian\nDefence Force Cover Act 2015.\nSubdivision B—Powers of AFCA"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1053a-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
