      "cml:premiseText": "funds and approved deposit funds and holders of RSAs",
      "cml:conclusionText": "taken to be a member of a regulated superannuation fund or an approved deposit fund, or a holder of an RSA"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1053a-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "is",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Non-member spouse obligation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) a non-member spouse in relation to whom a splitting order under the Family Law Act 1975 has been made, from the day on which a copy of the order is served on the trustee of the fund;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "taken to be a member of a regulated superannuation fund or an approved deposit fund"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1053a-logic-deontic-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "is",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Superannuation agreement obligation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) a non-member spouse who is a party to a superannuation agreement under the Family Law Act 1975, from the day on which a copy of the agreement is served on the trustee of the fund;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "taken to be a member of a regulated superannuation fund or an approved deposit fund"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1053a-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "is",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Marriage order obligation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(c) a party to a marriage in relation to which an order of a kind referred to in Part VIIIAA of the Family Law Act 1975 has been made, if the order relates to an interest in the fund;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "taken to be a member of a regulated superannuation fund or an approved deposit fund"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1053a-logic-deontic-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "is",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Eligible person obligation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(d) an eligible person, within the meaning of section 90MZB of the Family Law Act 1975, in relation to an interest of the member or holder in the fund;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "taken to be a member of a regulated superannuation fund or an approved deposit fund"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1054",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1054 Power to join other parties to superannuation complaint",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022c00235#sch-1-sec-1054"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2022c00235.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2022c00235.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "(1) AFCA may (subject to subsection 1056A(3)) at any time join, as a\nparty to a superannuation complaint made under the AFCA\nscheme, any of the following persons whom AFCA decides should\nbe a party to the complaint:\n\n(a) a person who has applied to become a party to the complaint;\n\n(b) a trustee of a regulated superannuation fund or an approved\ndeposit fund;\n\n(c) an insurer;\n\n(d) an RSA provider;\n\n(e) a superannuation provider;\n\nExternal dispute resolution  Schedule 1\nAmendments applying from the day after Royal Assent  Part 1\n\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Putting Consumers First—Establishment of the\nAustralian Financial Complaints Authority) Act 2018\nCompilation date: 10/08/2022\nRegistered: 25/08/2022\n\n(f) a person whom AFCA decides is responsible for determining\neither or both of the existence and the extent of a disability\n(whether total and permanent or otherwise), if the subject\nmatter of the complaint relates to a benefit in respect of the\ndisability, whether under a contract of insurance or\notherwise.\nNote:\nSection 1056A requires certain procedures to be followed before a\nperson can be joined as a party to a superannuation complaint about a\ndecision relating to the payment of a death benefit.\n\n(2) If AFCA decides under subsection (1) that a person should be a\nparty to the complaint, AFCA must give the new party, and all of\nthe existing parties to the complaint, written notice of the decision\nand of the reasons for the decision.\n\n(3) If AFCA decides that a person who has applied to become a party\nto the complaint should not be a party to the complaint, AFCA\nmust give the person written notice of the decision and of the\nreasons for the decision.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) AFCA may (subject to subsection 1056A(3)) at any time join, as a\nparty to a superannuation complaint made under the AFCA\nscheme, any of the following persons whom AFCA decides should\nbe a party to the complaint:\n\n(a) a person who has applied to become a party to the complaint;\n\n(b) a trustee of a regulated superannuation fund or an approved\ndeposit fund;\n\n(c) an insurer;\n\n(d) an RSA provider;\n\n(e) a superannuation provider;\n\nExternal dispute resolution  Schedule 1\nAmendments applying from the day after Royal Assent  Part 1\n\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Putting Consumers First—Establishment of the\nAustralian Financial Complaints Authority) Act 2018\nCompilation date: 10/08/2022\nRegistered: 25/08/2022\n\n(f) a person whom AFCA decides is responsible for determining\neither or both of the existence and the extent of a disability\n(whether total and permanent or otherwise), if the subject\nmatter of the complaint relates to a benefit in respect of the\ndisability, whether under a contract of insurance or\notherwise.\nNote:\nSection 1056A requires certain procedures to be followed before a\nperson can be joined as a party to a superannuation complaint about a\ndecision relating to the payment of a death benefit.\n\n(2) If AFCA decides under subsection (1) that a person should be a\nparty to the complaint, AFCA must give the new party, and all of\nthe existing parties to the complaint, written notice of the decision\nand of the reasons for the decision.\n\n(3) If AFCA decides that a person who has applied to become a party\nto the complaint should not be a party to the complaint, AFCA\nmust give the person written notice of the decision and of the\nreasons for the decision.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1054-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1054-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1054-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b441e29092b703b62d89759b3f92f39f96d5fbe5390aa5b0de6ac0678aa80331"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022c00235#sch-1-sec-1054",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1054 Power to join other parties to superannuation complaint",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 24,
      "values:originalText": "(1) AFCA may (subject to subsection 1056A(3)) at any time join, as a\nparty to a superannuation complaint made under the AFCA\nscheme, any of the following persons whom AFCA decides should\nbe a party to the complaint:\n\n(a) a person who has applied to become a party to the complaint;\n\n(b) a trustee of a regulated superannuation fund or an approved\ndeposit fund;\n\n(c) an insurer;\n\n(d) an RSA provider;\n\n(e) a superannuation provider;\n\nExternal dispute resolution  Schedule 1\nAmendments applying from the day after Royal Assent  Part 1\n\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Putting Consumers First—Establishment of the\nAustralian Financial Complaints Authority) Act 2018\nCompilation date: 10/08/2022\nRegistered: 25/08/2022\n\n(f) a person whom AFCA decides is responsible for determining\neither or both of the existence and the extent of a disability\n(whether total and permanent or otherwise), if the subject\nmatter of the complaint relates to a benefit in respect of the\ndisability, whether under a contract of insurance or\notherwise.\nNote:\nSection 1056A requires certain procedures to be followed before a\nperson can be joined as a party to a superannuation complaint about a\ndecision relating to the payment of a death benefit.\n\n(2) If AFCA decides under subsection (1) that a person should be a\nparty to the complaint, AFCA must give the new party, and all of\nthe existing parties to the complaint, written notice of the decision\nand of the reasons for the decision.\n\n(3) If AFCA decides that a person who has applied to become a party\nto the complaint should not be a party to the complaint, AFCA\nmust give the person written notice of the decision and of the\nreasons for the decision."
    },
