    {
      "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1054b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1054B Power to require attendance at conciliation conferences",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022c00235#sch-1-sec-1054b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2022c00235.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2022c00235.pdf, p.26",
      "values:originalText": "(1) AFCA may, if AFCA thinks it desirable to do so, by notice in\nwriting given to:\n\n(a) each party to a superannuation complaint; and\n\n(b) any other person:\n\n(i) who, in AFCA’s opinion, is likely to be able to provide\ninformation relevant to the settlement of the complaint;\nor\n\n(ii) whose presence at a conciliation conference would, in\nAFCA’s opinion, be likely to be conducive to settling\nthe complaint;\nrequire the party or other person to attend the conference.\nNote:\nA strict liability offence may apply under section 1058 (secrecy) in\nrelation to information acquired during a conference held under this\nsection.\n\n(2) The notice must also fix the date, time and place for the\nconference.\n\nExternal dispute resolution  Schedule 1\nAmendments applying from the day after Royal Assent  Part 1\n\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Putting Consumers First—Establishment of the\nAustralian Financial Complaints Authority) Act 2018\nCompilation date: 10/08/2022\nRegistered: 25/08/2022\n\n(3) If the complainant fails to attend the conference, AFCA may deal\nwith the complaint as if it had been withdrawn by the complainant.\n\n(4) A person (other than the complainant) commits an offence if he or\nshe does not attend a conference when required to do so under this\nsection.\nPenalty: 30 penalty units.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) AFCA may, if AFCA thinks it desirable to do so, by notice in\nwriting given to:\n\n(a) each party to a superannuation complaint; and\n\n(b) any other person:\n\n(i) who, in AFCA’s opinion, is likely to be able to provide\ninformation relevant to the settlement of the complaint;\nor\n\n(ii) whose presence at a conciliation conference would, in\nAFCA’s opinion, be likely to be conducive to settling\nthe complaint;\nrequire the party or other person to attend the conference.\nNote:\nA strict liability offence may apply under section 1058 (secrecy) in\nrelation to information acquired during a conference held under this\nsection.\n\n(2) The notice must also fix the date, time and place for the\nconference.\n\nExternal dispute resolution  Schedule 1\nAmendments applying from the day after Royal Assent  Part 1\n\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Putting Consumers First—Establishment of the\nAustralian Financial Complaints Authority) Act 2018\nCompilation date: 10/08/2022\nRegistered: 25/08/2022\n\n(3) If the complainant fails to attend the conference, AFCA may deal\nwith the complaint as if it had been withdrawn by the complainant.\n\n(4) A person (other than the complainant) commits an offence if he or\nshe does not attend a conference when required to do so under this\nsection.\nPenalty: 30 penalty units.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1054b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1054b-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1054b-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1054b-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "245cecfaccb2030b0830ea0420053861929d75f8fea99d3ca2a753d265e52cbc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022c00235#sch-1-sec-1054b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1054B Power to require attendance at conciliation conferences",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 26,
      "values:originalText": "(1) AFCA may, if AFCA thinks it desirable to do so, by notice in\nwriting given to:\n\n(a) each party to a superannuation complaint; and\n\n(b) any other person:\n\n(i) who, in AFCA’s opinion, is likely to be able to provide\ninformation relevant to the settlement of the complaint;\nor\n\n(ii) whose presence at a conciliation conference would, in\nAFCA’s opinion, be likely to be conducive to settling\nthe complaint;\nrequire the party or other person to attend the conference.\nNote:\nA strict liability offence may apply under section 1058 (secrecy) in\nrelation to information acquired during a conference held under this\nsection.\n\n(2) The notice must also fix the date, time and place for the\nconference.\n\nExternal dispute resolution  Schedule 1\nAmendments applying from the day after Royal Assent  Part 1\n\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Putting Consumers First—Establishment of the\nAustralian Financial Complaints Authority) Act 2018\nCompilation date: 10/08/2022\nRegistered: 25/08/2022\n\n(3) If the complainant fails to attend the conference, AFCA may deal\nwith the complaint as if it had been withdrawn by the complainant.\n\n(4) A person (other than the complainant) commits an offence if he or\nshe does not attend a conference when required to do so under this\nsection.\nPenalty: 30 penalty units."
    },
