    {
      "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1054c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1054C Reference of questions of law to Federal Court",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022c00235#sch-1-sec-1054c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2022c00235.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2022c00235.pdf, p.27",
      "values:originalText": "(1) AFCA may, on its own initiative or on the request of a party to a\nsuperannuation complaint, refer a question of law arising in\nrelation to the making of a determination relating to the complaint\nto the Federal Court for decision.\n\n(2) The Federal Court has jurisdiction to hear and determine a question\nof law referred to it under this section.\n\n(3) If a question of law has been so referred to the Federal Court,\nAFCA must not:\n\nSchedule 1  External dispute resolution",
      "skos:definition": "(1) AFCA may, on its own initiative or on the request of a party to a\nsuperannuation complaint, refer a question of law arising in\nrelation to the making of a determination relating to the complaint\nto the Federal Court for decision.\n\n(2) The Federal Court has jurisdiction to hear and determine a question\nof law referred to it under this section.\n\n(3) If a question of law has been so referred to the Federal Court,\nAFCA must not:\n\nSchedule 1  External dispute resolution",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1054c-ss-1"
