      "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1055-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1055(4) Making a determination",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022c00235#sch-1-sec-1055-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2022c00235.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2022c00235.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "(4) If AFCA is satisfied that:\n\nExternal dispute resolution  Schedule 1\nAmendments applying from the day after Royal Assent  Part 1\n\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Putting Consumers First—Establishment of the\nAustralian Financial Complaints Authority) Act 2018\nCompilation date: 10/08/2022\nRegistered: 25/08/2022\n\n(a) a decision (except a decision relating to the payment of a\ndeath benefit), in its operation in relation to the complainant;\nor\n\n(b) conduct;\nis unfair or unreasonable, or both, AFCA may take any one or\nmore of the actions mentioned in subsection (6), but only for the\npurpose of placing the complainant, as nearly as practicable, in\nsuch a position that the unfairness, unreasonableness, or both, no\nlonger exists.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) If AFCA is satisfied that:\n\nExternal dispute resolution  Schedule 1\nAmendments applying from the day after Royal Assent  Part 1\n\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Putting Consumers First—Establishment of the\nAustralian Financial Complaints Authority) Act 2018\nCompilation date: 10/08/2022\nRegistered: 25/08/2022\n\n(a) a decision (except a decision relating to the payment of a\ndeath benefit), in its operation in relation to the complainant;\nor\n\n(b) conduct;\nis unfair or unreasonable, or both, AFCA may take any one or\nmore of the actions mentioned in subsection (6), but only for the\npurpose of placing the complainant, as nearly as practicable, in\nsuch a position that the unfairness, unreasonableness, or both, no\nlonger exists.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1055"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1055-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1055-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "78c2ae2c7c4f9e34d451b3681293c77367f73c7d770a816f05dd9c9a73189620",
      "skos:note": "AFCA may take actions to place a complainant in a position where unfairness or unreasonableness no longer exists."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022c00235#sch-1-sec-1055-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1055(4) Making a determination",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 28,
      "values:originalText": "(4) If AFCA is satisfied that:\n\nExternal dispute resolution  Schedule 1\nAmendments applying from the day after Royal Assent  Part 1\n\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Putting Consumers First—Establishment of the\nAustralian Financial Complaints Authority) Act 2018\nCompilation date: 10/08/2022\nRegistered: 25/08/2022\n\n(a) a decision (except a decision relating to the payment of a\ndeath benefit), in its operation in relation to the complainant;\nor\n\n(b) conduct;\nis unfair or unreasonable, or both, AFCA may take any one or\nmore of the actions mentioned in subsection (6), but only for the\npurpose of placing the complainant, as nearly as practicable, in\nsuch a position that the unfairness, unreasonableness, or both, no\nlonger exists."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1055-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1055-ss-4"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1055-ss-4-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "may",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to take actions",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "AFCA has the power to act",
      "cml:conclusionText": "AFCA must take actions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1055-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1055(5) Making a determination",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022c00235#sch-1-sec-1055-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2022c00235.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2022c00235.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "(5) If AFCA is satisfied that a decision relating to the payment of a\ndeath benefit, in its operation in relation to:\n\n(a) the complainant; and\n\n(b) any other person joined under subsection 1056A(3) as a party\nto the complaint;\nis unfair or unreasonable, or both, AFCA may take any one or\nmore of the actions mentioned in subsection (6), but only for the\npurpose of placing the complainant (and any other person so joined\nas a party), as nearly as practicable, in such a position that the\nunfairness, unreasonableness, or both, no longer exists.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) If AFCA is satisfied that a decision relating to the payment of a\ndeath benefit, in its operation in relation to:\n\n(a) the complainant; and\n\n(b) any other person joined under subsection 1056A(3) as a party\nto the complaint;\nis unfair or unreasonable, or both, AFCA may take any one or\nmore of the actions mentioned in subsection (6), but only for the\npurpose of placing the complainant (and any other person so joined\nas a party), as nearly as practicable, in such a position that the\nunfairness, unreasonableness, or both, no longer exists.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1055"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1055-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1055-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1126d0a7b9b439e8e94fb8d8888260bc362705941593aa6b5267d27acb174d69",
      "skos:note": "AFCA may take actions to place complainant in a position where unfairness/unreasonableness no longer exists."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022c00235#sch-1-sec-1055-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1055(5) Making a determination",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 28,
      "values:originalText": "(5) If AFCA is satisfied that a decision relating to the payment of a\ndeath benefit, in its operation in relation to:\n\n(a) the complainant; and\n\n(b) any other person joined under subsection 1056A(3) as a party\nto the complaint;\nis unfair or unreasonable, or both, AFCA may take any one or\nmore of the actions mentioned in subsection (6), but only for the\npurpose of placing the complainant (and any other person so joined\nas a party), as nearly as practicable, in such a position that the\nunfairness, unreasonableness, or both, no longer exists."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1055-ss-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1055-ss-5"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1055-ss-5-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "AFCA has an obligation to take actions.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1055-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1055(6) Making a determination",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022c00235#sch-1-sec-1055-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2022c00235.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2022c00235.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "(6) AFCA may, under subsection (4) or (5), do any of the following:\n\n(a) vary the decision;\n\n(b) set aside the decision and:\n\n(i) substitute a decision for the decision so set aside; or\n\n(ii) remit the decision to the person who made it for\nreconsideration in accordance with any directions or\nrecommendations of AFCA;\n\n(c) if the complainant was unfairly or unreasonably admitted into\na life policy fund:\n\n(i) require a party to the complaint to repay all money, or\nparticular money, received under the life policy to\nwhich the complaint relates; or\n\n(ii) set aside the whole or part of the terms or conditions of\nthe life policy in their application to the complainant; or\n\n(iii) vary the governing rules of the life policy fund in their\napplication to the complainant; or\n\nSchedule 1  External dispute resolution",
      "skos:definition": "(6) AFCA may, under subsection (4) or (5), do any of the following:\n\n(a) vary the decision;\n\n(b) set aside the decision and:\n\n(i) substitute a decision for the decision so set aside; or\n\n(ii) remit the decision to the person who made it for\nreconsideration in accordance with any directions or\nrecommendations of AFCA;\n\n(c) if the complainant was unfairly or unreasonably admitted into\na life policy fund:\n\n(i) require a party to the complaint to repay all money, or\nparticular money, received under the life policy to\nwhich the complaint relates; or\n\n(ii) set aside the whole or part of the terms or conditions of\nthe life policy in their application to the complainant; or\n\n(iii) vary the governing rules of the life policy fund in their\napplication to the complainant; or\n\nSchedule 1  External dispute resolution",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1055"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1055-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1055-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1055-ss-6-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3eaaf9021aa36ac75eb286ef58e8c151d925a384e5da20341fb93776bc56a7a8",
      "skos:note": "AFCA may vary or set aside a decision, and require repayment of money received under the life policy."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022c00235#sch-1-sec-1055-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1055(6) Making a determination",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 28,
      "values:originalText": "(6) AFCA may, under subsection (4) or (5), do any of the following:\n\n(a) vary the decision;\n\n(b) set aside the decision and:\n\n(i) substitute a decision for the decision so set aside; or\n\n(ii) remit the decision to the person who made it for\nreconsideration in accordance with any directions or\nrecommendations of AFCA;\n\n(c) if the complainant was unfairly or unreasonably admitted into\na life policy fund:\n\n(i) require a party to the complaint to repay all money, or\nparticular money, received under the life policy to\nwhich the complaint relates; or\n\n(ii) set aside the whole or part of the terms or conditions of\nthe life policy in their application to the complainant; or\n\n(iii) vary the governing rules of the life policy fund in their\napplication to the complainant; or\n\nSchedule 1  External dispute resolution"
    },
