        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) a superannuation complaint has been made concerning a disability benefit (whether under a contract of insurance or otherwise);",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The person must comply with any determination made in respect of the person by AFCA."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1055d-logic-ltl-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "BETWEEN",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Temporal interval between complaint and commencement",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) a superannuation complaint has been made concerning a disability benefit (whether under a contract of insurance or otherwise);",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The person must comply with any determination made in respect of the person by AFCA."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1055d-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to comply with determination",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(c) AFCA joins the person under subsection 1054(1) as a party to the complaint;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The person must comply with any determination made in respect of the person by AFCA."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1056a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1056A Joining persons to complaints relating to death benefit",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022c00235#sch-1-sec-1056a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2022c00235.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2022c00235.pdf, p.33",
      "values:originalText": "decisions\n\n(1) If a death benefit decision-maker:\n\n(a) makes a decision relating to the payment of a death benefit;\nand\n\n(b) is notified by AFCA of a superannuation complaint made in\naccordance with section 1056 relating to the decision;\nthe decision-maker must, within 28 days after being so notified,\ngive notice to each person (other than the complainant) whom the\ndecision-maker believes, after reasonable enquiry, may have an\ninterest in the death benefit.\n\n(2) A notice given to a person under subsection (1) must:\n\n(a) state that a complaint has been made to AFCA about the\ndecision; and\n\n(b) set out the details of the complaint; and\n\n(c) state that the person may apply to be joined as a party to the\ncomplaint by giving notice to AFCA within 28 days after the\nperson is given notice, or such longer period as AFCA\nallows.\n\n(3) A person (other than a person referred to in any of paragraphs\n1054(1)(b) to (f)) may be joined as a party to the complaint under\nsection 1054 only if:\n\n(a) the person applies in accordance with paragraph (2)(c) of this\nsection; or\n\n(b) AFCA is satisfied that, in all the circumstances, the person\nshould be joined as a party despite not so applying.\nSubdivision E—Appeals to the Federal Court",
      "skos:definition": "decisions\n\n(1) If a death benefit decision-maker:\n\n(a) makes a decision relating to the payment of a death benefit;\nand\n\n(b) is notified by AFCA of a superannuation complaint made in\naccordance with section 1056 relating to the decision;\nthe decision-maker must, within 28 days after being so notified,\ngive notice to each person (other than the complainant) whom the\ndecision-maker believes, after reasonable enquiry, may have an\ninterest in the death benefit.\n\n(2) A notice given to a person under subsection (1) must:\n\n(a) state that a complaint has been made to AFCA about the\ndecision; and\n\n(b) set out the details of the complaint; and\n\n(c) state that the person may apply to be joined as a party to the\ncomplaint by giving notice to AFCA within 28 days after the\nperson is given notice, or such longer period as AFCA\nallows.\n\n(3) A person (other than a person referred to in any of paragraphs\n1054(1)(b) to (f)) may be joined as a party to the complaint under\nsection 1054 only if:\n\n(a) the person applies in accordance with paragraph (2)(c) of this\nsection; or\n\n(b) AFCA is satisfied that, in all the circumstances, the person\nshould be joined as a party despite not so applying.\nSubdivision E—Appeals to the Federal Court",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1056a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1056a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1056a-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3183d37be5060278b0f0b2ea1095fea98e027d276f661719821018f5511f4927"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022c00235#sch-1-sec-1056a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1056A Joining persons to complaints relating to death benefit",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 33,
      "values:originalText": "decisions\n\n(1) If a death benefit decision-maker:\n\n(a) makes a decision relating to the payment of a death benefit;\nand\n\n(b) is notified by AFCA of a superannuation complaint made in\naccordance with section 1056 relating to the decision;\nthe decision-maker must, within 28 days after being so notified,\ngive notice to each person (other than the complainant) whom the\ndecision-maker believes, after reasonable enquiry, may have an\ninterest in the death benefit.\n\n(2) A notice given to a person under subsection (1) must:\n\n(a) state that a complaint has been made to AFCA about the\ndecision; and\n\n(b) set out the details of the complaint; and\n\n(c) state that the person may apply to be joined as a party to the\ncomplaint by giving notice to AFCA within 28 days after the\nperson is given notice, or such longer period as AFCA\nallows.\n\n(3) A person (other than a person referred to in any of paragraphs\n1054(1)(b) to (f)) may be joined as a party to the complaint under\nsection 1054 only if:\n\n(a) the person applies in accordance with paragraph (2)(c) of this\nsection; or\n\n(b) AFCA is satisfied that, in all the circumstances, the person\nshould be joined as a party despite not so applying.\nSubdivision E—Appeals to the Federal Court"
    },
    {
