        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "318f446b265fc43f656e27871bb589138209777f6ed460ae7ff113258ea7283c",
      "skos:note": "Notice to be given to persons with an interest in death benefit",
      "dc:description": "Notice"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022c00235#sch-1-sec-1056a-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1056A(1) Joining persons to complaints relating to death benefit",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 33,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a death benefit decision-maker:\n\n(a) makes a decision relating to the payment of a death benefit;\nand\n\n(b) is notified by AFCA of a superannuation complaint made in\naccordance with section 1056 relating to the decision;\nthe decision-maker must, within 28 days after being so notified,\ngive notice to each person (other than the complainant) whom the\ndecision-maker believes, after reasonable enquiry, may have an\ninterest in the death benefit."
