    {
      "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1057",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1057 Appeals to the Federal Court from determination of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022c00235#sch-1-sec-1057"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2022c00235.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2022c00235.pdf, p.33",
      "values:originalText": "superannuation complaint\n\n(1) A party to a superannuation complaint may appeal to the Federal\nCourt, on a question of law, from AFCA’s determination of the\ncomplaint.\n\nSchedule 1  External dispute resolution",
      "skos:definition": "superannuation complaint\n\n(1) A party to a superannuation complaint may appeal to the Federal\nCourt, on a question of law, from AFCA’s determination of the\ncomplaint.\n\nSchedule 1  External dispute resolution",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1057-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1057-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "21d98c481def9245993052e8922fa8f40eded91c025de0ed4590c5a4903ed1bd",
      "skos:note": "Party may appeal to Federal Court from AFCA's determination on a question of law."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022c00235#sch-1-sec-1057",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1057 Appeals to the Federal Court from determination of",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 33,
      "values:originalText": "superannuation complaint\n\n(1) A party to a superannuation complaint may appeal to the Federal\nCourt, on a question of law, from AFCA’s determination of the\ncomplaint.\n\nSchedule 1  External dispute resolution"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1057-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1057"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1057-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "may",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to appeal",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1057a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1057A Operation and implementation of determination that is",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022c00235#sch-1-sec-1057a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2022c00235.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2022c00235.pdf, p.34",
      "values:originalText": "subject to appeal\n\n(1) Subject to this section, the institution of an appeal to the Federal\nCourt from AFCA’s determination of a superannuation complaint\ndoes not affect the operation of the determination or prevent the\ntaking of action to implement the determination.\n\n(2) If an appeal is brought to the Federal Court from the determination,\nthe Court or a Judge of the Court may make such order or orders\nstaying or otherwise affecting the operation or implementation of\neither or both of the following:\n\n(a) the determination or a part of the determination;\n\n(b) if the complaint relates to a decision of another person—the\nwhole or part of the decision that is complained of, or of a\ndecision of an insurer or other person who is a party to the\ncomplaint;\n\nExternal dispute resolution  Schedule 1\nAmendments applying from the day after Royal Assent  Part 1\n\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Putting Consumers First—Establishment of the\nAustralian Financial Complaints Authority) Act 2018\nCompilation date: 10/08/2022\nRegistered: 25/08/2022\n\nas the Court thinks appropriate to secure the effectiveness of the\nhearing and determination of the appeal.\n\n(3) If an order is in force under subsection (2) (including an order that\nhas previously been varied on one or more occasions under this\nsubsection), the Court or a Judge of the Court may make an order\nvarying or revoking the first-mentioned order.\n\n(4) An order in force under subsection (2) (including an order that has\npreviously been varied on one or more occasions under\nsubsection (3)):\n\n(a) is subject to such conditions as are specified in the order; and\n\n(b) has effect until:\n\n(i) if a period for the operation of the order is specified in\nthe order—the end of that period or, if a decision is\ngiven on the appeal before the end of that period, the\ngiving of the decision; or\n\n(ii) if no period is so specified—the giving of a decision on\nthe appeal.",
      "skos:definition": "subject to appeal\n\n(1) Subject to this section, the institution of an appeal to the Federal\nCourt from AFCA’s determination of a superannuation complaint\ndoes not affect the operation of the determination or prevent the\ntaking of action to implement the determination.\n\n(2) If an appeal is brought to the Federal Court from the determination,\nthe Court or a Judge of the Court may make such order or orders\nstaying or otherwise affecting the operation or implementation of\neither or both of the following:\n\n(a) the determination or a part of the determination;\n\n(b) if the complaint relates to a decision of another person—the\nwhole or part of the decision that is complained of, or of a\ndecision of an insurer or other person who is a party to the\ncomplaint;\n\nExternal dispute resolution  Schedule 1\nAmendments applying from the day after Royal Assent  Part 1\n\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Putting Consumers First—Establishment of the\nAustralian Financial Complaints Authority) Act 2018\nCompilation date: 10/08/2022\nRegistered: 25/08/2022\n\nas the Court thinks appropriate to secure the effectiveness of the\nhearing and determination of the appeal.\n\n(3) If an order is in force under subsection (2) (including an order that\nhas previously been varied on one or more occasions under this\nsubsection), the Court or a Judge of the Court may make an order\nvarying or revoking the first-mentioned order.\n\n(4) An order in force under subsection (2) (including an order that has\npreviously been varied on one or more occasions under\nsubsection (3)):\n\n(a) is subject to such conditions as are specified in the order; and\n\n(b) has effect until:\n\n(i) if a period for the operation of the order is specified in\nthe order—the end of that period or, if a decision is\ngiven on the appeal before the end of that period, the\ngiving of the decision; or\n\n(ii) if no period is so specified—the giving of a decision on\nthe appeal.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1057a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1057a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1057a-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1057a-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "135fbc3c74758a7211ede9c0d2cbe799ecfb8169e25a8bf5d8ca6294ff2d7f5a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022c00235#sch-1-sec-1057a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1057A Operation and implementation of determination that is",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 34,
      "values:originalText": "subject to appeal\n\n(1) Subject to this section, the institution of an appeal to the Federal\nCourt from AFCA’s determination of a superannuation complaint\ndoes not affect the operation of the determination or prevent the\ntaking of action to implement the determination.\n\n(2) If an appeal is brought to the Federal Court from the determination,\nthe Court or a Judge of the Court may make such order or orders\nstaying or otherwise affecting the operation or implementation of\neither or both of the following:\n\n(a) the determination or a part of the determination;\n\n(b) if the complaint relates to a decision of another person—the\nwhole or part of the decision that is complained of, or of a\ndecision of an insurer or other person who is a party to the\ncomplaint;\n\nExternal dispute resolution  Schedule 1\nAmendments applying from the day after Royal Assent  Part 1\n\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Putting Consumers First—Establishment of the\nAustralian Financial Complaints Authority) Act 2018\nCompilation date: 10/08/2022\nRegistered: 25/08/2022\n\nas the Court thinks appropriate to secure the effectiveness of the\nhearing and determination of the appeal.\n\n(3) If an order is in force under subsection (2) (including an order that\nhas previously been varied on one or more occasions under this\nsubsection), the Court or a Judge of the Court may make an order\nvarying or revoking the first-mentioned order.\n\n(4) An order in force under subsection (2) (including an order that has\npreviously been varied on one or more occasions under\nsubsection (3)):\n\n(a) is subject to such conditions as are specified in the order; and\n\n(b) has effect until:\n\n(i) if a period for the operation of the order is specified in\nthe order—the end of that period or, if a decision is\ngiven on the appeal before the end of that period, the\ngiving of the decision; or\n\n(ii) if no period is so specified—the giving of a decision on\nthe appeal."
    },
