      "cml:premiseText": "Court makes order staying or affecting operation of determination",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Order and determination overlap in time"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1057a-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "1057A(3) Operation and implementation of determination that is",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022c00235#sch-1-sec-1057a-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2022c00235.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2022c00235.pdf, p.34",
      "values:originalText": "(3) If an order is in force under subsection (2) (including an order that\nhas previously been varied on one or more occasions under this\nsubsection), the Court or a Judge of the Court may make an order\nvarying or revoking the first-mentioned order.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) If an order is in force under subsection (2) (including an order that\nhas previously been varied on one or more occasions under this\nsubsection), the Court or a Judge of the Court may make an order\nvarying or revoking the first-mentioned order.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1057a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1057a-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1057a-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ef8c3bec955e967d221abddcfafbe365477b9fd49ea74994ec78b6225db472db",
      "skos:note": "May vary or revoke an existing order under subsection (2)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022c00235#sch-1-sec-1057a-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "1057A(3) Operation and implementation of determination that is",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 34,
      "values:originalText": "(3) If an order is in force under subsection (2) (including an order that\nhas previously been varied on one or more occasions under this\nsubsection), the Court or a Judge of the Court may make an order\nvarying or revoking the first-mentioned order."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-1057a-ss-3-norm",
