      "skos:note": "Dissatisfied person may make complaint under AFCA scheme or Superannuation (Resolution of Complaints) Act 1993."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022c00235#sch-1-sec-30",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "30 Subsection 390-5(1) in Schedule 1 (note 2)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 44,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the note, substitute:\nNote 2:\nIf a person is dissatisfied with a statement given to the Commissioner\nby a superannuation provider under this section, the person may make\na complaint:\n(a) under the AFCA scheme (within the meaning of Chapter 7 of the\nCorporations Act 2001), but not before the authorisation of the\nscheme comes into force; or\n(b) under section 15CA of the Superannuation (Resolution of\nComplaints) Act 1993, but not on or after the day on or after\nwhich complaints cannot be made because of section 14AB of\nthat Act."
    },
