    {
      "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-44",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44 Application of amendments",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022c00235#sch-1-sec-44"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2022c00235.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2022c00235.pdf, p.47",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe amendments made by this Part apply on and after the day that is:\n\n(a) the day specified under subitem (2); or\n\n(b) if no such day is specified—the day that is 12 months after\nthe day on which the first authorisation of an external dispute\nresolution scheme, under Part 7.10A of the Corporations Act\n2001 as amended by Part 1 of this Schedule, comes into\nforce.\n(2)\nThe Minister may, by notifiable instrument, specify a day for the\npurposes of paragraph (1)(a). The day must not be earlier than the day\non which the first authorisation of an external dispute resolution\nscheme, under Part 7.10A of the Corporations Act 2001 as amended by\nPart 1 of this Schedule, comes into force.\n\nSchedule 1  External dispute resolution",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nThe amendments made by this Part apply on and after the day that is:\n\n(a) the day specified under subitem (2); or\n\n(b) if no such day is specified—the day that is 12 months after\nthe day on which the first authorisation of an external dispute\nresolution scheme, under Part 7.10A of the Corporations Act\n2001 as amended by Part 1 of this Schedule, comes into\nforce.\n(2)\nThe Minister may, by notifiable instrument, specify a day for the\npurposes of paragraph (1)(a). The day must not be earlier than the day\non which the first authorisation of an external dispute resolution\nscheme, under Part 7.10A of the Corporations Act 2001 as amended by\nPart 1 of this Schedule, comes into force.\n\nSchedule 1  External dispute resolution",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-44-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-1-sec-44-logic-alleninterval-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1151eb7c25205cc189b26d4348ffaa87f03c9b43b104d3b8a36f91b70b5b3608",
      "skos:note": "Conditional commencement of amendments"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022c00235#sch-1-sec-44",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44 Application of amendments",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 47,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe amendments made by this Part apply on and after the day that is:\n\n(a) the day specified under subitem (2); or\n\n(b) if no such day is specified—the day that is 12 months after\nthe day on which the first authorisation of an external dispute\nresolution scheme, under Part 7.10A of the Corporations Act\n2001 as amended by Part 1 of this Schedule, comes into\nforce.\n(2)\nThe Minister may, by notifiable instrument, specify a day for the\npurposes of paragraph (1)(a). The day must not be earlier than the day\non which the first authorisation of an external dispute resolution\nscheme, under Part 7.10A of the Corporations Act 2001 as amended by\nPart 1 of this Schedule, comes into force.\n\nSchedule 1  External dispute resolution"
    },
    {
