      },
      "dc:source": "c2022c00235.pdf, p.56",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) particular financial products are, or have been, available for\nacquisition (whether by issue or sale) by a person or persons\nas retail clients; and\n\n(b) the issue or sale of those products is not covered by an\nAustralian financial services licence;\nboth the issuer, and any regulated person obliged under\nsubsection 1012C(5), (6) or (8) to give a retail client a Product\nDisclosure Statement for one or more of those financial products,\nmust each:\n\n(c) have a dispute resolution system complying with\nsubsection (2); and\n\n(d) give to ASIC the same information as the issuer or regulated\nperson would be required to give under\nsubparagraph 912A(1)(g)(ii) of that Act if the issuer or\nregulated person were a financial services licensee.\nNote 1:\nIf the issue of particular financial products is covered by an Australian\nfinancial services licence, the requirement to have a dispute resolution\nsystem relating to the issue of the products is imposed by\nparagraph 912A(1)(g).\n\nInternal dispute resolution  Schedule 2\n\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Putting Consumers First—Establishment of the\nAustralian Financial Complaints Authority) Act 2018\nCompilation date: 10/08/2022\nRegistered: 25/08/2022\n\nNote 2:\nFailure to comply with this subsection is an offence (see\nsubsection 1311(1)).\nNational Consumer Credit Protection Act 2009",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) particular financial products are, or have been, available for\nacquisition (whether by issue or sale) by a person or persons\nas retail clients; and\n\n(b) the issue or sale of those products is not covered by an\nAustralian financial services licence;\nboth the issuer, and any regulated person obliged under\nsubsection 1012C(5), (6) or (8) to give a retail client a Product\nDisclosure Statement for one or more of those financial products,\nmust each:\n\n(c) have a dispute resolution system complying with\nsubsection (2); and\n\n(d) give to ASIC the same information as the issuer or regulated\nperson would be required to give under\nsubparagraph 912A(1)(g)(ii) of that Act if the issuer or\nregulated person were a financial services licensee.\nNote 1:\nIf the issue of particular financial products is covered by an Australian\nfinancial services licence, the requirement to have a dispute resolution\nsystem relating to the issue of the products is imposed by\nparagraph 912A(1)(g).\n\nInternal dispute resolution  Schedule 2\n\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Putting Consumers First—Establishment of the\nAustralian Financial Complaints Authority) Act 2018\nCompilation date: 10/08/2022\nRegistered: 25/08/2022\n\nNote 2:\nFailure to comply with this subsection is an offence (see\nsubsection 1311(1)).\nNational Consumer Credit Protection Act 2009",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-2-sec-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-2-sec-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bef18b6baf3555faded7e301e87c3d99a476052ae439aebde6c83ea3869ecfeb",
      "skos:note": "Mandatory dispute resolution system for issuers and regulated persons",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022c00235#sch-2-sec-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 Subsection 1017G(1)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 56,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) particular financial products are, or have been, available for\nacquisition (whether by issue or sale) by a person or persons\nas retail clients; and\n\n(b) the issue or sale of those products is not covered by an\nAustralian financial services licence;\nboth the issuer, and any regulated person obliged under\nsubsection 1012C(5), (6) or (8) to give a retail client a Product\nDisclosure Statement for one or more of those financial products,\nmust each:\n\n(c) have a dispute resolution system complying with\nsubsection (2); and\n\n(d) give to ASIC the same information as the issuer or regulated\nperson would be required to give under\nsubparagraph 912A(1)(g)(ii) of that Act if the issuer or\nregulated person were a financial services licensee.\nNote 1:\nIf the issue of particular financial products is covered by an Australian\nfinancial services licence, the requirement to have a dispute resolution\nsystem relating to the issue of the products is imposed by\nparagraph 912A(1)(g).\n\nInternal dispute resolution  Schedule 2\n\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Putting Consumers First—Establishment of the\nAustralian Financial Complaints Authority) Act 2018\nCompilation date: 10/08/2022\nRegistered: 25/08/2022\n\nNote 2:\nFailure to comply with this subsection is an offence (see\nsubsection 1311(1)).\nNational Consumer Credit Protection Act 2009"
    },
