    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-2-sec-9",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9 Subsections 101(1) and (1A)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022c00235#sch-2-sec-9"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2022c00235.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2022c00235.pdf, p.58",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\n\n(1) Each trustee of a regulated superannuation fund other than a self\nmanaged superannuation fund, or of an approved deposit fund:\n\n(b) must have an internal dispute resolution procedure that\ncomplies with the standards, and requirements, mentioned in\nsubparagraph 912A(2)(a)(i) of the Corporations Act 2001 in\nrelation to financial services licensees; and\n\n(c) must give to ASIC the same information as the trustee would\nbe required to give under subparagraph 912A(1)(g)(ii) of the\nCorporations Act 2001 if the trustee were a financial services\nlicensee; and\n\n(d) must ensure that written reasons are given, in accordance\nwith requirements specified under subsection (1B) of this\n\nInternal dispute resolution  Schedule 2\n\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Putting Consumers First—Establishment of the\nAustralian Financial Complaints Authority) Act 2018\nCompilation date: 10/08/2022\nRegistered: 25/08/2022\n\nsection, for any decision of the trustee (or failure by the\ntrustee to make a decision) relating to a complaint.\nNote:",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\n\n(1) Each trustee of a regulated superannuation fund other than a self\nmanaged superannuation fund, or of an approved deposit fund:\n\n(b) must have an internal dispute resolution procedure that\ncomplies with the standards, and requirements, mentioned in\nsubparagraph 912A(2)(a)(i) of the Corporations Act 2001 in\nrelation to financial services licensees; and\n\n(c) must give to ASIC the same information as the trustee would\nbe required to give under subparagraph 912A(1)(g)(ii) of the\nCorporations Act 2001 if the trustee were a financial services\nlicensee; and\n\n(d) must ensure that written reasons are given, in accordance\nwith requirements specified under subsection (1B) of this\n\nInternal dispute resolution  Schedule 2\n\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Putting Consumers First—Establishment of the\nAustralian Financial Complaints Authority) Act 2018\nCompilation date: 10/08/2022\nRegistered: 25/08/2022\n\nsection, for any decision of the trustee (or failure by the\ntrustee to make a decision) relating to a complaint.\nNote:",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-2-sec-9-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2022c00235-sch-2-sec-9-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c618daa6fabba6a0e58db27fb5d5186b8992273ec324c9e1f785c1d96f9c6b2b",
      "skos:note": "Trustees of regulated superannuation funds must have an internal dispute resolution procedure and provide certain information to ASIC.",
      "dc:description": "Internal dispute resolution procedure, written reasons for decisions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2022c00235#sch-2-sec-9",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9 Subsections 101(1) and (1A)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 58,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\n\n(1) Each trustee of a regulated superannuation fund other than a self\nmanaged superannuation fund, or of an approved deposit fund:\n\n(b) must have an internal dispute resolution procedure that\ncomplies with the standards, and requirements, mentioned in\nsubparagraph 912A(2)(a)(i) of the Corporations Act 2001 in\nrelation to financial services licensees; and\n\n(c) must give to ASIC the same information as the trustee would\nbe required to give under subparagraph 912A(1)(g)(ii) of the\nCorporations Act 2001 if the trustee were a financial services\nlicensee; and\n\n(d) must ensure that written reasons are given, in accordance\nwith requirements specified under subsection (1B) of this\n\nInternal dispute resolution  Schedule 2\n\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Putting Consumers First—Establishment of the\nAustralian Financial Complaints Authority) Act 2018\nCompilation date: 10/08/2022\nRegistered: 25/08/2022\n\nsection, for any decision of the trustee (or failure by the\ntrustee to make a decision) relating to a complaint.\nNote:"
    },
